// BDE -> FireDAC conversion library -- a STARTING POINT, not a finished rule book.
//
// Assembled 2026-08-02 from convrules\FireDAC_Migrate_BDE.rules (Embarcadero's
// reFind corpus, imported verbatim and NOT modified). That corpus is 60 flat
// #migrate lines; this file re-expresses the part of it the ConvRules editor can
// work with -- one #convert block per component pair, with the property links
// filled in -- and carries the rest through unchanged at the bottom.
//
// WHAT IS CORPUS-SUPPLIED (trust it): every #unuse and #remove line, the units on
//   each #convert header, both #mapping blocks, and the #link lines under a
//   '#note corpus' marker. These come from Embarcadero's own migration rules.
//
// WHAT IS MACHINE-GENERATED (review it): the #link lines under a
//   '#note auto-matched' marker. They were produced by the editor's own Auto-Match
//   rule, replayed headlessly against `drag-lint proptree --min-visibility
//   published --refs-as-leaves` for both sides (library-Win64 index): a source
//   leaf is paired only when exactly ONE writable, still-unassigned target leaf
//   has the same FULL PATH and a legal cast; failing that, only when the source
//   leaf's NAME is unique among ALL target last-segments and exactly one such
//   target is castable. Nothing ambiguous was guessed.
//
// EVERY SOURCE PROPERTY CARRIES A DIRECTIVE. A property that got no target is
//   not silently absent: it gets a block-scoped '#ignore <FromPath>', which is the
//   documented way to say 'intentionally NOT mapped'. On top of that, a property
//   that is unmapped in EVERY block exposing it and read by NO #link anywhere also
//   gets a machine-derived file-scope '#remove' in section 1, so it is stripped
//   from the result rather than carried over dead.
//
// A '#remove' is only derived when it is provably safe. '#remove' is FILE-SCOPED
//   and takes a BARE property name -- it has no '<Class>:' qualifier the way
//   #migrate does -- so it hits every component in the converted file. Three
//   things therefore BLOCK a derived #remove, each flagged by its own #note:
//
//   * '#note CONFLICT'      -- unmapped here, but #link'd in another block (or by
//                              a sub-property of the same name in this one).
//                              Removing it would strip it from under that link.
//   * '#note NEAR-MISS'     -- unmapped, but THIS target still HAS the property;
//                              Auto-Match only declined because the two type names
//                              do not bridge (TableName is TFileName on BDE and
//                              String on FireDAC). These are unresolved MAPPINGS,
//                              not deletions -- #remove'ing one would silently
//                              destroy a live property. Link them by hand.
//   * '#note NAME COLLISION'-- no counterpart on this target, but another block's
//                              target has a property of that name.
//
// '#remove X' AND '#remove DFM: X' ARE NOT THE SAME STATEMENT -- do not conflate
//   them, in this file or when you extend it:
//     #remove X       strips X from BOTH the .pas and the .dfm. X is GONE. It is
//                     a decision, it settles the property, and X must not also
//                     be #link'd. (Corpus: SessionName, PrivateDir.)
//     #remove DFM: X  drops ONLY the value persisted in the .dfm and KEEPS the
//                     property in code. It is NOT evidence that X is unassigned:
//                     it must not suppress a #link, and it does not count toward
//                     the outstanding total. (Corpus: Origin -- the one DFM-only
//                     line in the corpus, and Origin IS #link'd, on purpose.)
//
// WHAT STILL NEEDS A HUMAN, in priority order:
//   * every '#note NEAR-MISS' line -- these are the cheapest real wins: the target
//     property exists and is named, so each is one hand-made #link;
//   * every '#note CONFLICT' and '#note NAME COLLISION' line -- a judgement call;
//   * The #migrate lines at the bottom could not become property links -- they
//     rename METHODS (Session.*, FindDatabase, AddAlias, TDatabase:Execute), or
//     enum types with no property that carries them (TUpdateKind, TUpdateAction,
//     TDBScreenCursors), or classes with no published surface at all
//     (TBlobStream, EDBEngineError). They are carried VERBATIM, not dropped.
//   * convert-apply does not evaluate #mapping/#apply yet (DSL doc, Known limits
//     #1), so a post-save `convert-validate` reports those two directives as
//     unknown. The file is correct; the engine has not caught up.
//
// Unit/file renames (uAD.inc -> FireDAC.inc and 210 more) are a DIFFERENT domain
// and are deliberately NOT merged here -- see convrules\FireDAC_Rename_Units.rules.
//
// Plain 7-bit ASCII, CRLF.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 1. BDE units to drop (corpus, verbatim)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#unuse BDE.DBTables
#unuse BDE.BDEConst
#unuse DBTables
#unuse BDEConst
#unuse BDEMTS
#unuse BDE

// Corpus, verbatim: properties with no FireDAC counterpart at all.
#remove SessionName
#remove PrivateDir
#remove DFM: Origin

// MACHINE-DERIVED (not corpus): each property below is unmapped in EVERY
// #convert block that exposes it, and NO #link anywhere reads it, so stripping
// it file-wide cannot pull the rug from under another block. Each one also
// carries a block-scoped #ignore at its own #convert, so the intent is stated
// twice on purpose: #ignore says 'not mapped', #remove says 'and delete it'.
// NOTE #remove is FILE-SCOPED and takes a BARE property name -- it has no
// '<Class>:' qualifier -- so a generically-named entry here (Source,
// Destination, Mappings, ...) will also strip that property from any OTHER
// component in the converted file. Delete the ones you are not sure about.
#remove AbortOnKeyViol
#remove AbortOnProblem
#remove AutoRefresh
#remove AutoSessionName
#remove ChangedTableName
#remove Constrained
#remove DefaultIndex
#remove Destination
#remove HandleShared
#remove HasConstraints
#remove IndexFiles
#remove KeepConnections
#remove KeyViolTableName
#remove NetFileDir
#remove OnPassword
#remove OnStartup
#remove ParamCheck
#remove ProblemTableName
#remove Ranged
#remove RecordCount
#remove SQLHourGlass
#remove StoreDefs
#remove TableType
#remove Transliterate

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 2. Enum-valued property conversions (corpus). Only the two groups that a
//    #convert block below actually consumes are expressed as #mapping; the
//    other three enum groups have no property carrying them and stay #migrate.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#mapping BdeTransIsolation from Bde.DBTables.TTransIsolation to FireDAC.Comp.Client.TFDConnection
#mapping BdeTransIsolation #when TransIsolation = tiDirtyRead -> TxOptions.Isolation = xiDirtyRead
#mapping BdeTransIsolation #when TransIsolation = tiReadCommitted -> TxOptions.Isolation = xiReadCommitted
#mapping BdeTransIsolation #when TransIsolation = tiRepeatableRead -> TxOptions.Isolation = xiRepeatableRead

#mapping BdeBatchMode from Bde.DBTables.TBatchMode to FireDAC.Comp.BatchMove.TFDBatchMove
#mapping BdeBatchMode #when Mode = batAppend -> Mode = dmAppend
#mapping BdeBatchMode #when Mode = batUpdate -> Mode = dmUpdate
#mapping BdeBatchMode #when Mode = batAppendUpdate -> Mode = dmAppendUpdate
#mapping BdeBatchMode #when Mode = batDelete -> Mode = dmDelete
#mapping BdeBatchMode #when Mode = batCopy -> Mode = dmAlwaysInsert

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// 3. Component conversions
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

#convert Bde.DBTables.TSession -> FireDAC.Comp.Client.TFDManager, FireDAC.Comp.Client
#note 11 source properties: 0 corpus-supplied, 3 auto-matched, 0 via #mapping,
#note 8 unmapped -- every one of them named in an #ignore below, none silent.
#note auto-matched by the editor's Auto-Match rule -- review before applying.
#link Active <- Active
#link Name <- Name
#link Tag <- Tag
#note unmapped -- each line below is a decision, not an omission:
#note - 6 also #remove'd file-wide (unmapped everywhere, read by no #link).
#note - 2 already decided by the corpus's own file-scope #remove -- NOT
#note - counted as work, and deliberately not #remove'd a second time.
#ignore AutoSessionName
#ignore KeepConnections
#ignore NetFileDir
#ignore PrivateDir
#ignore SessionName
#ignore SQLHourGlass
#ignore OnPassword
#ignore OnStartup

