//    (e) class pairs that are TYPE renames, not component conversions: an
//        abstract base class or a non-component, with no usable published
//        property surface on one or both sides. Measured 2026-08-02 against
//        the Win64 library index, at --min-visibility published:
//          TBlobStream / TFDBlobStream           0 leaves both sides
//          EDBEngineError / EFDDBEngineException 0 leaves both sides
//          TDBDataSet (64) / TBDEDataSet (57) -> FireDAC.Comp.Client.TFDRdbmsDataSet:
//            the TARGET publishes only Name and Tag of its own (every other
//            member is public and re-published by the concrete TFDQuery/TFDTable
//            descendants instead). Auto-Match against it produced 57 links, of
//            which 52 were identity links into shared Data.DB metadata
//            sub-objects (FieldDefs.*, Constraints.*, FieldDefList.*) -- true
//            but worthless, since those are the SAME Data.DB classes on both
//            sides -- 4 were Name/Tag, and ONE was demonstrably wrong,
//            'Indexes.Items.Filter <- Filter'. A #convert block was written and
//            then withdrawn on that evidence. Convert the CONCRETE class
//            (TQuery/TTable/TStoredProc) instead; this line stays a type rename.
#migrate TBlobStream -> TFDBlobStream, FireDAC.Comp.DataSet
#migrate EDBEngineError -> EFDDBEngineException, FireDAC.Stan.Error
#migrate TDBDataSet -> TFDRDBMSDataSet, FireDAC.Comp.Client
#migrate TBDEDataSet -> TFDRDBMSDataSet, FireDAC.Comp.Client
